\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443833 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443833 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119461" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443833 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443833 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{6}{7}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443833 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "118e7fad-b51e-5b1f-8cd6-2d517d8a5df9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443833 #edb/ref 1074 "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{2-6}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-6$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/67/6709a58db6cc2c9d5b5811282fcf34d5d6766b7dba9f9f46db5cabacbd90f95d.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-6}{7}=\\frac{-4}{7}=-\\frac{4}{7}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443834 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443834 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119549" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443834 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443834 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{3}-1\\,\\frac{1}{9}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443834 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1599934d-a927-5358-9a1f-a60248bbf5f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443834 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{9}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{(1\\times 9)+1}{9}=\\frac{10}{9}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{1}{3}$ as $-\\frac{3}{9}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{9}-\\frac{10}{9}=\\frac{-3-10}{9}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-3-10$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f2/f27b92c1bbd62f5cba5fc75a4205034a24fb0298e77a662d6c59203dd42a2760.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-3-10}{9}=\\frac{-13}{9}=-\\frac{13}{9}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{13}{9}=-1\\,\\frac{4}{9}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443835 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443835 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443835 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443835 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $-\\frac{3}{11}-\\frac{6}{11}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443835 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e29b1c7-106c-5ab0-8d9e-819610a3356d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443835 #edb/ref 1074 "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{11}-\\frac{6}{11}=\\frac{-3-6}{11}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-3-6$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/24/24970f00ebf3ea583b8cd56831990f5d501ecaf1c87091e194c02ee7ecc0ff70.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{-3-6}{11}=\\frac{-9}{11}=-\\frac{9}{11}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443836 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443836 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119559" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443836 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443836 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $2\\,\\frac{3}{4}-3\\,\\frac{1}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443836 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38a15d99-3414-508c-84b1-39ed573baedb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443836 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write $2\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{(2\\times 4)+3}{4}=\\frac{11}{4}\n$$\n\nWe also write $3\\,\\frac{1}{4}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{(3\\times 4)+1}{4}=\\frac{13}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our problem now is to work out the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{4}-\\frac{13}{4}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{4}-\\frac{13}{4}=\\frac{11-13}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $11-13$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/be/befeb1f1947d5325530ac772fcf1411b04ae74bd78e377dc3eff547461a87627.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{11-13}{4}=\\frac{-2}{4}=-\\frac{2}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{4}=-\\frac{2÷2}{4÷2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443837 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443837 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119389" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443837 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443837 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{7}{6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443837 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "39ba11e1-e910-5353-9445-994f4bc57a7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443837 #edb/ref 1074 "We write $\\frac{2}{3}$ as $\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{7}{6}=\\frac{4-7}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/d5/d542609ee447bff7bcb3209bb8ea6eccbd770509d2ae4ad794df9eb6606c2b17.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-7}{6}=\\frac{-3}{6}=-\\frac{3}{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{6}=-\\frac{3÷3}{6÷3}=-\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{7}{6}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443838 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443838 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119508" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443838 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443838 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{1}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443838 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d3c4be6-4f0d-589b-961f-38e5107411d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443838 #edb/ref 1074 "We write $\\frac{2}{7}$ as $\\frac{6}{21}$ and $\\frac{1}{3}$ as $\\frac{7}{21},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{21}-\\frac{7}{21}=\\frac{6-7}{21}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $6-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/f3/f39be0767b6d9b5c3203946adc4212201c49cd6539cfc49c3c75646d7ea4bac5.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{6-7}{21}=\\frac{-1}{21}=-\\frac{1}{21}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443839 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443839 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119464" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443839 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443839 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of $\\frac{4}{11}-\\frac{9}{11}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443839 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53cf2acb-145a-5506-896e-6068ff12e934" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443839 #edb/ref 1074 "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{11}-\\frac{9}{11}=\\frac{4-9}{11}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/3f/3f5b60548cfd0332c74508678de51481f9fa149466c7d7880217b905e4d3891a.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-9}{11}=\\frac{-5}{11}=-\\frac{5}{11}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443840 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443840 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119552" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443840 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443840 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{1}{5}-1\\,\\frac{3}{10}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443840 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "841f7692-e519-5922-bdbc-38496ec5b53f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443840 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{3}{10}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{(1\\times 10)+3}{10}=\\frac{13}{10}\n$$\n\nAlso, we write $-\\frac{1}{5}$ as $-\\frac{2}{10}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{10}-\\frac{13}{10}=\\frac{-2-13}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-2-13$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/65/651e46f49551c462bbf15db5e1fc554aa0ff81d7f81fc64286f15c226be69800.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-2-13}{10}=\\frac{-15}{10}=-\\frac{15}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we simplify:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{15}{10}=-\\frac{15÷5}{10÷5}=-\\frac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}=-1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443841 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443841 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42713" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443841 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443841 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443841 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d8f39de-a2f7-5903-8fdc-c4a3db5001e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443841 #edb/ref 1074 "We write $\\frac{1}{2}$ as $\\frac{2}{4}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}-\\frac{7}{4}=\\frac{2-7}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/ee/eea536f581897431a30a8bdadabe7d02fc1f5fc783af2221fda4b2e7f9d6d936.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-7}{4}=\\frac{-5}{4}=-\\frac{5}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443842 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443842 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443842 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443842 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the value of $-\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{7}{10}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443842 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9177f11e-16b2-5f25-b1c3-d0c370d0a589" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443842 #edb/ref 1074 "We write $-\\frac{2}{5}$ as $-\\frac{4}{10}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{4}{10}-\\frac{7}{10}=\\frac{-4-7}{10}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-4-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](images/d2/d2965f3b03382313757e12920c55ca04be14bf5ae8d5957a15458f5548b8402d.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-4-7}{10}=\\frac{-11}{10}=-\\frac{11}{10}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443843 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186443822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443843 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101213" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186443843 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 1759218